  "because": "The widest value of every axis over every occupant that runs a process, and here all four code occupants carry the same block -- the tightest one the library ships. The fifth occupant is a `store` and spawns nothing, so it widens no axis; its reach is `db:own` and lives in its own contract. The sixth is the `submit` hive, whose own occupants carry their own block in their own template -- a ref does not widen this file, it brings its own. Nothing in this hive fetches, executes a caller's string or reads a path: the four cells parse a request, format a message and emit it. That is the honest reading of what handing this hive a request can set in motion, and it is written down so that a replacement is measured against it: an occupant that needs more than this is, visibly, a widening in the diff of this file. The REACH of the hive is a different fact and lives where reach belongs -- in `params.contract`, on the `mutate`, `ask` and `export` lanes."
