    "reentrant": true,

      "because": "A ref onto the `submit` template, whose own gate keeps one row per submission in flight in the store beside it and pops them in FIFO order -- the mutation door is serial, so submission order and answer order are the same. The verdict is declared here because a hole in this table cannot catch a swap that quietly turns a parallel round sequential; what backs it lives in that template and not in this file."
    },
    "export": {
      "reentrant": true,
      "because": "It turns an address into a message. Nothing is held between two exports, and which member each one names travels in its own message."
    },
    "lifecycle": {
      "reentrant": true,
      "because": "It composes one declaration out of one request and keeps nothing. Two lifecycle changes in flight are two manifests, and their ORDER is the mutation door's to decide -- the same reading `intake` carries, one composition step earlier."
